From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: WM_MOUSEHWHEEL has no non-client form and carries screen coordinates

process_mouse_message exempted WM_MOUSEWHEEL alone from the non-client
translation: WM_MOUSEHWHEEL got client coordinates in lParam (Windows gives
both wheel messages the pointer in screen coordinates, and programs --
Chromium first -- ScreenToClient them, so a tilt wheel's or a touchpad's
sideways scroll went to the wrong point), and over the caption or a border
it became message 0x28c with the hit-test code for its wParam: the delta was
lost and nothing handled it. Found looking at the wheel path for GitHub #11.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -2606,8 +2606,18 @@
     pt = msg->pt;
     message = msg->message;
     wparam = msg->wParam;
-    /* Note: windows has no concept of a non-client wheel message */
+    /* Note: windows has no concept of a non-client wheel message.
+     * Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9510): nor of a non-client horizontal wheel
+     * message -- WM_MOUSEHWHEEL, like WM_MOUSEWHEEL, carries the pointer in
+     * screen coordinates wherever it is over the window. It came in client
+     * coordinates (programs ScreenToClient the lParam of both: Chromium
+     * scrolled the wrong element sideways) and over the caption became
+     * message 0x28c, which nothing handles. */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_HWHEEL_NONCLIENT
     if (message != WM_MOUSEWHEEL)
+#else
+    if (message != WM_MOUSEWHEEL && message != WM_MOUSEHWHEEL)
+#endif
     {
         if (hittest != HTCLIENT)
         {
